## Test Anti-Pattern Audit — Severity-Ranked Findings

This test suite is a textbook case of **"coverage theater"** — every production method is called (achieving line coverage), but almost nothing is actually verified. Here are the findings:

---

### 🔴 CRITICAL — Missing Assertions (coverage touching, zero verification)

**1. `AddProduct_Works` (line 17)** — Fire-and-forget, no assertion at all.
```csharp
// FIX: verify the product was actually persisted
_catalog.AddProduct(product);
var stored = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNotNull(stored);
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", stored.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, stored.Price);
```

**2. `UpdatePrice_Works` (line 32)** — Calls `UpdatePrice` but never checks the price changed.
```csharp
// FIX: assert the price was updated
_catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);
var updated = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, updated!.Price);
```

**3. `RemoveProduct_Works` (line 38)** — Calls `RemoveProduct` but never checks the product is gone.
```csharp
// FIX: assert the product no longer exists
_catalog.RemoveProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNull(_catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001"));
```

**4. `GetProductCount_Works` (line 63)** — No products added, count is never asserted. This would pass even if `GetProductCount` returned -1.
```csharp
// FIX: verify count reflects actual state
Assert.AreEqual(0, _catalog.GetProductCount());
_catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
Assert.AreEqual(1, _catalog.GetProductCount());
```

**5. `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` (line 68)** — Applies a 10% discount but never checks any price changed. A bug in the discount formula (e.g., `* fraction` instead of `* (1 - fraction)`) would pass silently.
```csharp
// FIX: verify discounted prices
_catalog.ApplyBulkDiscount(0.10m);
Assert.AreEqual(8.991m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001")!.Price);
Assert.AreEqual(17.991m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-002")!.Price);
```

**6. `ImportFromCsv_Works` (line 84)** — Imports CSV but never checks the product was created.
```csharp
// FIX: verify the imported product
_catalog.ImportFromCsv("SKU-001,Widget,9.99");
var product = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNotNull(product);
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", product.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, product.Price);
```

---

### 🟠 HIGH — Weak Assertions (assert exists, not correctness)

